course: dictionary
lesson: 11417
title: Meaning of acidity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acidity is how acidic something is, or how strong an acid it is. Scientists measure it on the pH scale. Things with a pH below 7 are acidic, and the lower the number, the stronger the acid. «The acidity of the lemon juice made my mouth pucker.» Here acidity means the sour taste that makes your face squeeze up.
explain: Acidity can also mean a burning feeling in your chest or stomach, called heartburn. «Dad had acidity after the spicy curry, so he took a tablet.» The word here is informal, so you will hear it more in everyday talk than in science books.
explain: Writers sometimes use acidity to mean sharpness or unkindness in words or manner. «The acidity in her reply made the whole class go quiet.» Clues like "made the class go quiet" tell you the reply was harsh, not that it tasted sour. Always check the context to find which meaning fits.
fact: Acidity means how strong an acid is.
fact: The pH scale runs from 0 to 14. Below 7 is acidic, 7 is neutral, and above 7 is alkaline.
fact: «Acidity» can mean the sour taste of food like lemons, or heartburn in the stomach.
fact: Scientists test acidity with litmus paper or red cabbage indicator. Litmus turns red in acidic liquids.
fact: Acid rain has high acidity and can harm lakes, forests and old stone buildings.
exercise: «The acidity of the lemon juice made my mouth pucker.» What does acidity mean here? | The sweet smell of the fruit | The bright colour of the juice | *The sour taste of the juice | Cold temperature of the drink
exercise: Scientists use litmus paper to test the «acidity» of a liquid. What does acidity tell them? | *How strong an acid the liquid is | How heavy the liquid is | How long the liquid lasts
exercise: Which pH number shows something is acidic? | 14 | 7 | *3 | 10
test: «Dad had acidity after the spicy curry, so he took a tablet.» What does acidity mean here? | Pain in the knee | A cold in the nose | Dizziness after running | *Heartburn in the stomach
test: «The acidity in her reply made the whole class go quiet.» What does acidity mean here? | *Sharp, unkind words | Loud singing | Warm and kind words | Quiet, soft whispers
exam: Which liquid has the most acidity? | Soap, pH 12 | Pure water, pH 7 | *Vinegar, pH 3 | Baking soda, pH 9
